"""A spelling-sensitive negative detector for Arabic MN, Russian iz and mon.

Arabic من (min, 'from/of') is strongest. Selected prefixed/suffixed fragments
also respond, whether or not they are prepositions. Comparisons ('more than'),
'despite', and quantity phrases change min's strength. Russian 'consists of'
is weaker than other uses of iz. Literal mon fragments and a few non-Latin
nasal spellings form a second cluster. This is not a universal semantic or
phonetic detector: unlisted spellings return zero. Only a short recent text
tail is retained, and it resets at document boundaries.
"""
