"""Names, files and paths: a token-level detector for the words "name" and "file".

Reads only the current token. It fires on the token that means a *name*, a *file*,
or a *path / folder* in code, config and prose, in any spelling: `name`, ` Name`,
`_NAME`, `.name`, `getName`, `filename`, `File`, `files`, `名`, `文件`, `path`, `dir`,
`folder`, `src`, `root`. Data-file extensions `.json`, `.yml`, `.yaml`, `.xml`, `.ts`
fire strongly; file-format words (`json`, `xml`, `typescript`, `README`) moderately;
package / module / resolve / ignore words weakly. Words that merely contain the
letters (`game`, `same`, `profile`, `director`, `username`) stay silent.

The token is split into its letter pieces (camelCase and snake_case split apart),
and the strongest family among its pieces sets the value.
