"""Collection relations, especially 'among', and partitive phrases like 'some of'.

Named prepositions receive negative responses. For 'of', the preceding
quantifier or membership noun determines the strength; punctuation and
capitalization distinguish sentence openings from ordinary phrases.
A smaller trace remains on a following article. Infinity notation and the
chastity/steadfastness characters 贞 and 貞 have separate positive responses.
These rules omit the component's many weaker, unrelated lexical responses.
"""
