"""A detector for written whitespace escapes, especially backslash-n.

Real newlines get zero. Written escapes get negative values, strongest
when the escape letter is a separate token. Repetition strengthens a
fused newline; extra backslashes weaken a split one. Nearby punctuation
makes small adjustments. This is an approximation, not a string parser.
"""
