A period/comma/question mark followed by a closing quote is positive. Quote
style, paragraph/code endings, and the amount of quoted text set its size.
Short quoted terms are weaker than full sentences. Activity words such as
'conduct', 'perform', 'undergo', and 'undertake' are negative; 'carry out'
is especially strong on 'out'. A few multilingual equivalents and split
spellings are included. Everything else is near zero. State is reset for
each document and remembers only the previous token/word and quote length.
